ain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  rightbreast mass with margins  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black  superiorly overlayed with green and sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal unremarkable fibrous tissue  Submitted almost entirely in cassettes A through J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two additional specimens  Labeled  right breast mass additional superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fatty adipose tissue which is inked and submitted entirely in cassettes K and L  Labeled  left breast  final shave margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes M through R  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm fragment of breast containing 2 sutures  Inked entirely in black  superior overlayed with green  and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm firm ill defined mass which is grossly focally present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes S through W from lateral to medial margin   S is the most lateral section  W is the most lateral margin  T through V are representative sections of the ill defined mass in relationship to the anterior and posterior margin   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two additional specimens Labeled  left breast mass  additional superficial margins  are multiple fragments of fatty adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes X and Y  Labeled  left breast  final shaved margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes Z through CC  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   2 CM INFILTRATING CARCINOMA FOCALLY PRESENT AT ANTERIOR MARGINS REMOVED_DATE CM FROM POSTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  PART D  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN  PART F  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  , Unchecked.
