erior aspect of the cavity which comes to 0 2cm of the inferior margin  0 7cm of the lateral  1 2cm of the medial  2 7cm of the superior  1 2cm of the posterior  and 3 5cm of the anterior margins  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic focus which comes to 0 6cm of the closest superior margin along the mid portion of the specimen  A localization wire is recovered separate in the specimen container  Representative sections are submitted from posterior to anterior as A H  with the posterior margin radially sectioned as A  the cavity as C D  and the hemorrhagic focus as H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  right axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes I J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm specimen of fibrofatty tissue  From this tissue multiple lymph nodes were dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Individual lymph nodes are submitted after sectioning  each in a single cassette  in cassettes K S  Additional lymph nodes are submitted whole in cassettes T U with five potential lymph nodes per cassette  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of tan pink soft tissue  Tissue fragments are sectioned and submitted in cassettes V W  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional inferior tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm specimen of tan white soft tissue which is sectioned and submitted in entirely in cassettes X Y  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  CHRISTO