Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 39 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma on core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR AND ANTERIOR MARGINS  SEE NOTE   2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   3  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS ADJACENT TO BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Definite angiolymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of ductal carcinoma in situ  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL LEVEL II   EXCISION  ALL 3 LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL 6 LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast CA   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast fragment with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm stellate  firm  tan pink mass  0 6cm from the superior  REMOVED_DATE from the lateral  0 8cm from the anterior  and 1 0cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is predominantly fatty  The tumor is submitted entirely along with margins as follows  A B  radial sections to superior margin  C  anterior and lateral margins  with lateral surface overinked blue  D  posterior and anterior margins  posterior surface overinked blue  E  other tumor sections   br , Unchecked.
