ssed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  One specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  stitch marks superior aspect  and consists of a 23 x 14 x 3cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a stitch marking the superior aspect and containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm irregular skin ellipse containing a nipple and a 2 5cm curvilinear scar  7 2cm lateral to the nipple  The specimen is inked and cross sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm hard mass beneath the scar  with an inhomogeneous tan yellow  cystic and brown cut surface  and abutting the anterior skin  The mass is greater than 1 5cm from the deep margin  Sections of the tumor are submitted in A through E  from medial to lateral  with B and C containing anterior superior margins and D and E containing anterior margins  There is 4 x 2 x 2cm area inferior and lateral to the mass which is firm and gray white  and abutting the inferior  anterior margin  Representative sections in F and G  1 5cm medial to the tumor is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm firm  white area  1 2cm from the nearest margin  anterior   Representative section is in H  Sectioning the tissue away from the mass reveals unremarkable fatty and white soft parenchyma  Representative sections are in I and J  with J in the area of the nipple  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in K through U  Please note that M contains a single node  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  M