r  and  right sentinel node   is a 3 x 2 x 0 4cm piece of fatty tissue containing a single lymph node  The lymph node is frozen entirely FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining portion of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of soft tissue containing a lymph node which is dissected free and frozen entirely as FX 2  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RIGHT SENTINEL NODE  BLUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  130   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART F  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  PART G  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLI , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 AUG 98 at 09 31 CLINICAL DATA  Status post three prior benign biopsies  Ill defined hypoechoic shadowing mass on ultrasound    scar tissue vs  carcinoma in area of palpable lump  Right breast mass at 10 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite angiolymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 AUG 98 at 20 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 5 pink tan soft tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in aggregate  The specimen is submitted in toto in Cassette A  Resident  QUN DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES , Unchecked.
