esults of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right modified mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE attached piece of overlying skin with nipple  The nipple is inverted  There is also attached axillary contents measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular hard  tan white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm  The lesion extends to within 1 7cm of the deep margin  The closest margin is the superficial margin  skin   where the closest distance is 1 0cm  The parenchyma surrounding the mass is yellow  fibrofatty tissue which is grossly unremarkable  There is another area of firmness in the white fibrous tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm located 4 0cm from the deep margin and 1 5cm from the superficial margin which has the overlying skin  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Dissected from the axillary fat are multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 7cm in diameter  Section code  A C  mass with superficial margin  closest margin  D E  area of white firmness F  section of inverted nipple G L  axillary lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm piece of overlying skin with nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white nodule with a small area of punctate hemorrhage in the middle  The firm white nodule is 4 5cm from the deep margin which is the closest margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the nodule is yellow fibrofatty tissue which is grossly unremarkable  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of the nodule are submitted in cassettes M thorough O and representative sections of normal breast parenchyma are submitted in cassettes P V  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
