Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 AUG 93 at 11 02 CLINICAL DATA  Lobular carcinoma of breast  posterior margins on lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  70   AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH EXTENSIVE PAGETOID SPREAD  30    DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH HEMORRHAGE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  GRANULATION TISSUE FORMATION AND FAT NECROSIS  NOTE  The inked deep and lateral resection margins are free of carcinoma  No axillary lymph nodes are received in the pathology department either with the specimen or separately submitted  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  18 AUG 93 at 07 42 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a mastectomy specimen consisting of a right breast  29 x 22 x 6 5cm  and overlying almost circular skin ellipse  27 x 21cm  without any obvious axillary tail  The whole specimen weighs  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram  8 5cm lateral to the nipple  as indicated by the surgeon  is a 4 5cm long curved  retracted  healing incision  Beneath this is an 8cm in largest diameter cystic cavity filled with blood clot  This cavity appears to be well circumscribed by a fibrous capsule and is 2cm from the deep resection margin  and 5cm from the lateral end of the skin  Up to 1cm wide area surrounding the cavity is tan yellow  firm  and gelatinous  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and contains mostly soft  yellow adipose tissue   The nipple is unremarkable   No lymph nodes are identified  SECTION CODE  A  deep margin B E  representative sections from the wall of the cystic cavity F L  representative sections of the firmer areas of the breast from the near the cystic cavity to medial end K M  nipple  and representative skin N  healed skin O Q  representative sections from the lateral area towards the tail  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Steven A Kagan  M D  Martine marie Dupic  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Paul N Staats  Reports To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  positive margins  old ruptured silicone implant  Stitches short superior  long lateral  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  IN THE REGION OF THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND  0 2 CM FROM MARGINS  2  PERIPROSTHETIC CAPSULE WITH HISTIOCYTIC REACTION TO FOREIGN MATERIAL  3  TWO AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  4  SILICONE LYMPHADENITIS  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm triangular portion of tan white skin with an unremarkable nipple  There is a long stitch on the skin designated lateral  and a short suture designated superior  The posterior surface is ruptured  A silicone implant is visible through the disruption  On removal  the implant is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm rubbery yellow tan cylinder with multiple disruptions and leaking gray white sticky material  There is lettering on the surface reading  McGhan  270cc   The mastectomy specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm fibrous walled cavity containing the implant and extravasated material consistent with silicone  Immediately anterior to this cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm biopsy cavity with surrounding tan white fibrous tissue and yellow tan firm areas  The biopsy cavity is directly underlying the skin ellipse  just medial and superior to the nipple  No residual mass is identified  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm area of tan white fibrous tissue in the central area of the breast just lateral to the skin ellipse  There is also an area of tan white fibrous tissue in the upper outer quadrant near the axillary tail  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of yellow tan fatty tissue and occasional tan pink and fibrous tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the upper outer quadrant  A photograph of the implant is taken  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative from central fibrous area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative from superior medial fibrous area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One large lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary fibrous area  Gross Dictation by Paul N Staats  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paul N Staats  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
