y five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan  breast biopsy with a hard  smooth nodule palpated beneath the adipose tissue  This specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  gray  poorly circumscribed lesion REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  abutting an inked resection margin  Submitted entirely in A through C  with lesion in A and B  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
