Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 08 CLINICAL DATA  67 year old female with carcinoma of the left breast  this is re excision of lump with axillary dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    RE EXCISION  1  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  2  FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  FAT NECROSIS WITH FOAMY HISTIOCYTES AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELLS CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA OR DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   ALL  19  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 17                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a 4 5cm overlying skin ellipse containing a 3 5cm linear central scar  There is a long stitch and a short stitch  the long stitch designating medial is inked red and the short stitch designating inferior is inked blue  the remainder is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity with blood in the center and surrounding it firm  tan to yellow  poorly circumscribed tissue  The biopsy cavity is 2 0cm from the overlying skin ellipse and 2 0cm from the closest margin  medial   The remainder of the breast tissue is fibrofatty  Section code  A  biopsy cavity  deepest inferior margin B  biopsy cavity  deepest superior margin C  biopsy cavity including skin D  representative section of margin and inferior biopsy cavity E  representative section of closest medial  red ink  margin F  representative section of medial superior fibrofatty tissue G  representative section of fibrous area in the superior lateral area Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue sectioned to reveal multiple tan pink lymph nodes  representative sections submitted in cassettes H L  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Jeffrey Schapiro MD Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  MASS  LEFT BREAST   REEXCISION PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 51 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of t