aterally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of skin  remarkable for a 1 5cm well healed scar  and is oriented by a short suture designating the superior and long suture designating the lateral margins  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior black  and posterior blue  and is serially sectioned to reveal a centrally located  adjacent and underneath the ellipse of skin  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm blue dye injected cavitary lesion  surrounded by areas suspicious for fat necrosis  The cavity measures 0 9cm from the anterior and 0 8cm from superior deep margin   closest margin   The remainder of parenchyma is predominanatly yellow lobulated fatty tissue  also present medially is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm white  blue dye injected ill defined lesion which abuts the anterior and inferior margins  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODE  C  cavity with anterior and inferior margins  D G  cavitary lesion  entirely  H  skin with underlying breast tissue  adjacent to the cavity  I J  ill defined lesion  medial posterior inferior  Labelled  non sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan gray node with surrounding fatty tissue  bisected and submitted entirely as K L  Gross Description by  ALAN ALLBEE Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  FINAL SENTINEL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLA FINAL SENTINEL    EXCISIO PART C  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLA NON SENTINEL    EXCISION , Unchecke