Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram   calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  ATROPHY  AND CYST FORMATION  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  90   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN IN SMALL FOCI  AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  AND EXTENDING TO MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  CALCIFIED FIBROADENOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm white pink breast tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly white breast parenchyma  No area grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section done  Submitted entirely in A through J with area near tip of wire in B and C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of firm  yellow pink breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm nodule  a fine stellate white tissue with hemorrhagic streaks and calcifications near localizing wire  The nodule reaches the margin in multiple points  A section is frozen as FX 1  Submitted entirely in K through P  Frozen saved for Cox 5  Tissue submitted for Dr  Sgroi  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS ONLY   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY PART B  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  BOWES Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Resident  Ricard Masia  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Michiya Nishino  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 48 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma and lobular carcinoma in situ diagnosed by core biopsy of the left breast  A 1 7cm mass at 3 o clock was noted on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1    SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  3cm  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma is positive at the superior  medial and lateral margin of the specimen along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Sections of the main lumpectomy specimen reveal an invasive carcinoma with a main tumor mass measuring 1 7cm in maximum diameter  In addition to this main mass  there are many microscopic satellite nodules present suggesting a larger overall mass than the 1 7cm measured grossly  The tumor exhibits two distinct growth patterns  In some areas there is a distinct single file growth pattern characteristic of invasive lobular carcinoma  In other areas  the tumor infiltrates in small angulated nests  typical of tubular carcinoma  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin were performed on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The e cadherin stain is negative in areas of invasive lobular growth pattern and positive in areas of tubular growth pattern  The e cadherin stain is also negative in areas of LCIS and positive in areas of DCIS  The immunohistochemical staining pattern supports the morphologic findings  Thus the overall impression is that of an invasive tubulo lobular carcinoma  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL AXILLARY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1   BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT AT THE MARGIN OF RESECTION  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE   Note  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin is negative in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  Multiple level sections were examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR LATERAL   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE TUBULO  LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  INVASIVE TUBULO LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS 