ith a 1 2cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  which extends to within 1 7cm of the skin margin  The specimen has a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm slightly raised tan red lesion on the skin  which extends to within 1 6cm of the nearest  12 o clock  margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm cavity  consistent with a previous biopsy site  which is located in the upper inner quadrant of the specimen and extends to within 1 0cm of the nearest posterior margin  The cavity is surrounded by dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal areas of tan yellow fat necrosis  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrous tissue and fat necrosis  with the entire cavity submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue at the lateral aspect of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire skin lesion  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1 AND FX 1A   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART C  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Unchecked.
