Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 94 at 16 04 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass with fine needle aspiration positive for malignancy  needs ER and PR                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  97    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR SURGICAL RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  4  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE WITH DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE CHANGE AND MICROCYSTS  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   ELEVEN OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE IS NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  09 MAY 94 at 17 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of p