terone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy with needle localization wire   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a needle localizing wire in place  and an accompanying specimen X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal adipose tissue interspersed with white  rubbery  fibrous tissue  There is no grossly suspicious lesion for infiltrating carcinoma identified  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted with possible microcalcifications in A through F and the remaining tissue entirely in G through Q  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  GROSS TUMOR MASS NOT IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION   report_end  , Unchecked.
