y biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 5 x 5 x 2cm portion of breast with a long stitch designating lateral  and a short stitch designating superior  The entire surface is inked black  with the superior half overinked blue  It is serially sectioned to reveal a 3 x 3 x 2cm gritty mass  focally abutting the anterior inferior inked margin  Firm white fibrous tissue extends away from this mass  and abuts the anterior medial superior margin  A representative section of the anterior medial superior margin is frozen as FX  1  now A  The mass also abuts the posterior margin  0 3cm medial to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm cyst lined by white  fibrous tissue  Surrounding the cyst is white fibrous parenchyma with scattered microcysts  Lateral to the mass is mixed fibrous parenchyma with scattered cysts and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  anterior superior medial margin  B  Anterior superior medial margin  C D  Anterior inferior medial margin  E  Posterior margin  F H  Representative sections of mass  I J  Firm cystic area  medial to mass  K L  Fibrous cystic area  lateral to m