ith this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number in two parts  Labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of fibroadipose tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overlying skin ellipse  The deepest portion of the specimen is focally hard  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan  gritty mass that abuts the inked resection margin  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted as A  Representative portions of the tumor including the closest resection margin are submitted in B through E  A representative portion of the overlying skin is submitted in F  Representative portions of grossly unremarkable tissue is submitted in G through I  A gross photograph is taken  Labeled  new deep resection margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch marking the deepest portion  The deep margin is inked  the specimen is sectioned perpendicular to the long axis  and submitted entirely in J through N  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  POSSIBLY MEDULLARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  NEW DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
