Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right nipple duct excision  Rule out papilloma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT NIPPLE DUCT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1 TO FOCAL 2  WITH FOCUS HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR EARLY INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  One slightly irregular focus of carcinoma almost completely lacks a myoepithelial cell layer  as seen on p63  smooth muscle myosin  and calponin immunostains  A cytokeratin stain highlights the irregularities in contour  This area spans about 0 1cm and is favored to represent early blunt invasion arising out of ductal carcinoma in situ  Other nests of carcinoma also demonstrate large gaps in the myoepithelial cell layer  perhaps representing an earlier stage of the same phenomenon  The ductal carcinoma in situ involves 8 of 12 blocks and is focally positive at the inked margin  as well as being  0 1cm from the inked margin along a broad front  Calcifications are present in the ductal carcinoma in situ and in vessels  Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right nipple duct rule out papilloma   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm excisional breast biopsy specimen consisting of tan yellow  lobulated fatty tissue with focal hemorrhage 