Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Christopher K Hysell  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  64 year old female with invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE SEE NOTE  NOTE  Stains for p63 protein  calponin  keratin  and myosin heavy chain do not disclose carcinoma  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed  labeled  Cynthia Norton  REMOVED_DATE  right breast  is a 910 gram simple mastectomy specimen  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10 3cm ellipse of skin with an unremarkable nipple  The surgeon denotes the axillary tail with a suture  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity with variegated  yellow red and tan discoloration of the surrounding tissue  The cavity extends to 0 7cm from the anterior margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and greater than 5 0cm from the remaining margins  1 0cm lateral to the cavity there is a 0 7cm region of yellow red discoloration of the fat  1 0cm medial and 5 0cm superior  in the 12 o clock region  is a 0 4cm tan nodule  which is greater than 3 0cm from all margins  Lymph nodes are not identified in the axillary tail  The following cassettes are submitted  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative posterior margin  underlying the cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity with relationship to anterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue lateral to the biopsy cavity such that this discoloration is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in the 12 o clock region such that it is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from cavity from the medial aspect of the specimen with posterior margin included   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from the cavity from the lateral aspect of the specimen with posterior margin included  Fellow Review by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 12 29 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast cancer with DCIS at margins  stitch marks superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  EXTENSIVE RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  INVOLVING 9 OF 17 BLOCKS  AND PRESENT  0 2 CM FROM THE POSTERIOR AND ANTERIOR MARGINS ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Note  Ductal carcinoma in situ is extensively present throughout the specimen in the areas adjacent to and distant from the biopsy site  A micropapillary pattern similar to that of the previous specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   is seen within the DCIS  No definite stromal invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 05                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a 18 x 12 x 1 2cm simple mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and a suture on the superior margin  The nipple is unremarkable  There is a linear 3 5cm surgical scar located 2 5cm from the nipple at 1 o clock  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked green and the posterior surface black  Serially sectioning of the posterior margin reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  with a indurated tan brown wall and tan brown soft papillary projections into the cavity  The cavity is surrounded by fat necrosis and fibrous tissue and is directly subjacent to the linear scar on the skin surface  The anterior wall of the biopsy cavity has been previously opened  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm anterior defect  abutting the superior edge of the skin ellipse  The cavity is 0 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 0 6cm deep to the skin  The rest of the margins are  1 0cm from the cavity  Adjacent to  but distinct from the first cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic cavity which contains old blood and fibrin  located at 2 5cm away from the nipple at 5 o clock position  0 2cm from the posterior margin and 0 9cm from anterior margin  This cavity is also surrounded by fat necrosis and fibrous tissue  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fibrofatty without any additional focal lesions  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals 2 papable lymph nodes averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity to the anterior  posterior margins and skin surface  B C  Representative section of the biopsy cavity to the posterior  anterior margins and skin surface  D E  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity to anterior  posterior margins and skin surface  F  A representative section of the biopsy cavity to anterior margin and skin surface  G K  Representative sections of the smaller cavity to the posterior  and anterior margins  L M  Representative sections of breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the medial aspect of the specimen  N O  Representative sections of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the lateral aspect of the specimen  P  Representative sections of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the superior aspect of the specimen  Q  Representative section of the breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity from the inferior aspect of the specimen  R  Axillary lymph nodes  bisected  S  Representative section of the nipple  Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Isaac Schiff  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
