Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 59 CLINICAL DATA  Positive core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 1  MARGINS NEGATIVE  WITHOUT LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH COMEDO NECROSIS  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR FOR REMOVED_DATE CM  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  HOT SPOT   762   BIOPSY  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE LYMPH NODE   WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR SPREAD  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL I   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL II   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  HOT SPOT   523   BIOPSY  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE LYMPH NODE   WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR SPREAD  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Five containers are received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm mastectomy specimen with a overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  with a suture designating the superior aspect  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple is unremarkable  The tan skin is unremarkable  The specimen is breadloafed to reveal a nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in greatest dimension is approximately 2 0cm from the medial margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin  6 0cm from the superior margin and 15 0cm from the lateral margin  Section Code  A  farthest inferiomedial extension of tumor C  section through granular extension of lesion D  section through fibrous region of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm E  representative deep margin  nearest tumor F  additional section of deep margin  near fibrous area  Labeled  left axilla  low Hot Spot  1  CT 762   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm nodule of fatty tissue  Labeled  left axillary lymph  Level I   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fatty nodular tissue  H  one lymph node I N  additional lymph nodes  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  Level  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of fatty fibrous tissue  O  representative lymph node  Level  2 Labeled  left axilla  Hot Spot    CT  523   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty nodular tissue  Bisected and submitted entirely in P  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  LEFT AXILLA  HOT SPOT   762 PART C  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1  PART D  LEFT AXILLARY  LEVEL II  PART E  LEFT AXILLA  HOT SPOT  523    report_end  , Unchecked.
