ith a 2 0cm central scar  There is a small axillary tail which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The anterior surface is inked blue  and the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated tan white fibrotic scar which is adjacent to the previously mentioned skin ellipse with scar  The scar is adjacent to the anterior surface and the posterior surface  The remainder of the cut surface is tan white to tan yellow with the large areas of soft and rubbery fibrotic and unremarkable breast tissue  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes to reveal four possible lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 2cm to 0 6cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as labeled  B K  The entire excisional scar submitted in sequential fashion with the medial aspect in cassette B and the lateral aspect in cassette K  L M  Representative breast tissue away  N  Four possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary node  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral   is a 160 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm simple mastectomy specimen which is oriented by a short stitch designated superior and a long stitch designated lateral  The areola is REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and the unremarkable nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan red well delineated area in the upper inner quadrant which measures 0 6cm from the posterior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The remainder of the cut surface is tan white to tan yellow and fibrotic with multiple pin point tan yellow nodular areas  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of the fibrotic tissue that 