agnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cystic space containing a gray to tan yellow friable material  The cyst wall is gray pink  fibrous  and averages less than 0 1cm in thickness  The cystic structure focally abuts the postero inferior margin and comes to 1 0cm of the anterior  4 0cm of the superior  and more than 2cm of the medial and lateral margins  Abutting the cyst along the posterosuperior aspect  is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm indurated gray white lobulated mass which comes to 0 5cm of the posterior  1 2cm of the inferior  1 3cm of the anterior  3 7cm of the superior  and 1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margin  Along the anterosuperior aspect of the indurated lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic space containing a soft tan brown substance  The space is consistent with previous biopsy site and is surrounded by focal bright yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The space comes to 0 3cm of the anterior  REMOVED_DATE of the superior  2 0cm of the inferior  1 4cm of the posterior  1 7cm of the lateral  and greater than 2cm of the medial margins  One of the localization wires is located in the tissue immediately medial to the indurated lesion and cavity  The second localization wire is located 1 2cm medial to the first wire  The cross sections are taken to breast imaging and radiographed  The remaining dense gray white fibrous tissue shows focal gritty areas  Representative section is submitted  from medial to lateral  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region designated by second localization wire   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcification to superior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcifications   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area designated by localization wire  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire indurated lesion and representative hemorrhagic cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cystic structure  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative hemorrhagic cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible calcifications  NOTE  Please note radiographs accompany the specimen and are mapped according to tissue in the radiographs  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular portion of yellow fatty tissue  within which multiple tan pink candidate lymph nodes are identified  The candidate lymph nodes are submitted in entirety for frozen section as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two bisected candidate lymph nodes  both of which are inked   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple whole candidate lymph nodes and one bisected lymph node  inked black   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow pink irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a stitch designating the new margin  inked black   The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly yellow fatty cut surface  with focal yellow chalky areas  No lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  2  SENTINEL NODES  BIOPSY  CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORK UP  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on 