Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 28 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY   EXCISION  ALL  5  LYMPH NODES APPEAR FREE OF TUMOR  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  TWO FOCI REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL AND MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  RESPECTIVELY  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SCANT 3  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  5  ALL  17  LYMPH NODES APPEAR FREE OF TUMOR  NOTE  All margins appear free of tumor  Definite lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not seen  The two foci of carcinoma are physically located 4cm from one another and display different histomorphologic features  Therefore  these two carcinomas most likely represent independent primary neoplasms Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 36                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 21 x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 19 x 5cm tan skin ellipse containing a 2 0cm round unremarkable nipple areolar complex  and an attached REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a hard white stellate slightly gritty nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm which is 2 0cm from the posterior  closest  margin and greater than 5 0cm from all other margins  Located 3 0cm medial to that nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of fibrous irregularity containing multiple blue dome cysts measuring 0 2cm in greatest dimension  This fibrous area is 3 0cm from the closest  deep  margin  1 0cm medial to this is an additional area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm which is rough white and irregular and is 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  these areas have been described from medial to lateral  The remainder of the specimen is composed of fibroadipose tissue and scattered blue dome cysts measuring up to 0 2cm  No discrete biopsy cavity is identified  Section codes  A  medial most hard nodule with posterior margin B C  remainder of above nodule D  fibrous areas surrounding nodule E F  second area mentioned in gross  fibrous nodule G  third nodule and posterior margin H  remainder of third nodule I  area of white cysts 2 0cm inferior to the second nodule J K  uninvolved medial tissue L  uninvolved lateral tissue From the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified measuring in size up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative sections of lymph nodes are submitted in R V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superficial margin  upper outer quadrant   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue which is entirely submitted in M O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of yellow red fibroadipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm are identified and submitted as follows  Section code  P  representative sections of four lymph nodes Q  one lymph node entirely submitted Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL  PART B  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY  CONTENTS PART C  BREAST  LEFT   RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
