E     REMOVED_CASE_ID     left breast  left  modified radical mastectomy  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  5 9cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect  and long suture designating the lateral aspect  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 10 6cm  tan white skin ellipse is remarkable for a centrally located  mildly retracted  nipple areolar complex  with no additional visible skin changes  The anterior  margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The specimen is serially  sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm stellate  irregular  firm tan white  mass that appears centered subjacent to the nipple and extends throughout most  of the breast  The lateral aspect of the mass is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  4 0cm area of tan white fleshy change containing a ribbon shaped metal clip   An additional potential biopsy site is identified approximately 1 0cm medial to  the metal clip  The mass is located a closest distance of  0 1cm to the black  inked posterior margin  0 3cm to the closest blue inked anterior margin  3 5cm  from the medial most aspect of the specimen  7 0cm from the lateral most aspect  of the specimen  3 5cm to the superior most aspect of the specimen  and 0 3cm  to the inferior most aspect of the specimen  The remaining tissue consists of  fat and dense gray white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional masses or  lesions are identified  Multiple intact candidate lymph nodes are palpated in  the lateral tissue  The following representative sections are submitted     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lateral fleshy nodule within the large mass   to include area containing the clip in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and closest black inked posterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of mass  submitted from lateral to  medial  to include possible biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   closest blue inked anterior  margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and mass to areolar skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 intact candidate lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes each    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable breast parenchyma lateral to the mass     Additional sections were subsequently submitted as follows    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of tumor to areolar skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to lateral  grossly uninvolved skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact candidate lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary fat with potential lymph nodes     Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics  determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of  Pathology at Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or  approved by the U S Food and Drug Administration  FDA   the FDA has determined  that such clearance or approval is not necessary       PART   BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  LEFT       report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 30 CLINICAL DATA  Increasing calcifications on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   20    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  80   CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPES  MULTIFOCAL AND PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Estrogen receptors will be reported in an addendum     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES     INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODES  2  NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm red and yellow breast tissue fragment with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 4cm tan  firm  rubbery to gritty central region with faintly retracted borders  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through I  with the tan central region in A through D  Gross Description by  Douglas B  Flieder  MD Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND A MINUTE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR    0 4CM   TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
