om the lateral margin  0 2cm from the medial margin  8 0cm from the superior margin  and 1 5cm from the inferior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is notable for unremarkable fibro  fatty breast tissue  The suspicious area is submitted entirely  Labeled  axillary nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal nineteen lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 4 0cm in greatest dimension  The cut surfaces range from fleshy tan  to yellow  to white  SECTION CODE  A  superior margin  en face B  inferior margin  en face C  medial margin with mass  radial section D  lateral margin with mass  radial section E  anterior margin  radial section F  posterior margin  radial section G  mass with overlying skin H  mass  representative section I N  breast parenchyma  representative sections O U  axillary lymph nodes Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  AXILLARY   DISSECTION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of soft  tan cores  submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
